---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildWebAppSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import toolContent from '../../tools-content/compare.html?raw';

const appSchema = buildWebAppSchema({
  name: "Compare Airbrushes",
  description: "Put airbrush models side by side and compare specifications before buying.",
  path: "/tools/compare/",
  free: true,
});
---
<BaseLayout title="Compare Airbrushes | AirbrushDOC" description="Side-by-side comparison of popular airbrush models and specifications.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(appSchema)} />
  <main class="abd-container" style="padding: 40px 24px 80px;">
    <nav class="abd-breadcrumbs" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="abd-breadcrumbs-sep">›</span>
      <a href="/tools/">Tools</a>
      <span class="abd-breadcrumbs-sep">›</span>
      <span>Compare Airbrushes</span>
    </nav>
    <Fragment set:html={toolContent} />
  
    <section class="tool-about">
      <h2>How to use the airbrush comparison tool</h2>
      <p>Pick two or three airbrushes and the table lines up the specifications that actually
    change how they spray: needle and nozzle size, feed type, trigger action, and what the spares
    cost when something wears out.</p>
    <p>Needle size is the specification most people over-think. A 0.3&nbsp;mm needle covers the
    large majority of work, from miniatures to T-shirts, and only genuinely fine detail or heavy
    primer justifies moving away from it. Feed type matters more day to day: gravity feed suits
    small quantities and low pressure, siphon feed suits volume and quick colour changes.</p>
      <p class="tool-about-next"><strong>Read next:</strong> <a href="/blog/best-airbrush/">Best Airbrush 2026: tested picks for every budget</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.tool-about {
  max-width: 68ch;
  margin: 48px auto 0;
  padding: 28px 0 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--abd-border, #2a2a2a);
}
.tool-about h2 {
  font-family: var(--abd-font-display);
  font-size: 1.15rem;
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.tool-about p {
  color: var(--abd-text-dim);
  line-height: 1.75;
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.tool-about-next { margin-top: 18px; }
</style>
